1.LENGTH OF LINKED LIST
Given head of a singly linked list. Find the length of the linked list, where length is defined as the number of nodes in the linked list.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int getCount(Node head) {
                int count=0;
                Node temp=head;
                while(temp.next!=null){
                    count++;
                    temp=temp.next;
                }
                count++;
                return count;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/count-nodes-of-linked-list/1


2.LINKED LIST END INSERTION
You are given the head of a Singly Linked List and a value x, insert that value x at the end of the LinkedList and return the head of the modified Linked List.
SOURCE CODE : 
class Solution {
    public Node insertAtEnd(Node head, int x) {
        Node newnode=new Node(x);
        if(head==null){
            head=newnode;
            return head;
        }
        Node temp=head;
        while(temp.next!=null){
            temp=temp.next;
        }
        temp.next=newnode;
        return head;
    }
}
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/linked-list-insertion-1587115620/1


3.ATLEAST TWO GREATER
Given an array arr of distinct elements, the task is to return an array of all elements except the two greatest elements in sorted order.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public long[] findElements(long arr[]) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                long arr1[]=new long[arr.length-2];
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length-2;i++){
                    arr1[i]=arr[i];
                }
                return arr1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/at-least-two-greater-elements4625/1


4.KTH SMALLEST
Given an integer array arr[] and an integer k, find and return the kth smallest element in the given array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int kthSmallest(int[] arr, int k) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                return arr[k-1];
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/kth-smallest-element5635/1
